# ${SCREEN_NAME}/

Screen folder for `${SCREEN_NAME}`. Stamped from the `_screen_template/`.

## What lives here

| Subfolder | What lives here | File suffix |
| --- | --- | --- |
| [`components/`](components/) | Screen-local presentational components | `*.tsx` |
| [`hooks/`](hooks/) | Screen-local hooks | `use*.ts` |
| [`services/`](services/) | Business logic / API orchestration | `*.service.ts` |
| [`types/`](types/) | Types local to this screen | `*.types.ts` |

The screen component itself (e.g. `${SCREEN_NAME}Screen.tsx`) is the only
`.tsx` at the screen root.

## What does NOT live here

- Cross-screen UI primitives — those live in `${SRC_DIR}/components/`.
- Cross-screen hooks — those live in `${SRC_DIR}/hooks/`.
- API client wrappers — those live in `${SRC_DIR}/api/`.

## Next steps

1. Rename this folder to the screen name (e.g. `settings/`).
2. Create the `<Name>Screen.tsx` entry component at the screen root.
3. Register it in [`${SRC_DIR}/navigation/RootNavigator.tsx`](../../navigation/RootNavigator.tsx)
   and add the route to [`${SRC_DIR}/navigation/types.ts`](../../navigation/types.ts).
4. Fill the four subfolders. Each leaf is a `.gitkeep` placeholder.

